      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`fused_mul_mat_gguf` dispatches standard / K-quant GGUF matmuls to MMVQ (`ggml_mul_mat_vec_a8`) when `x.shape[0] <= mmvq_safe`, with `mmvq_safe = 2` for matrices with more than 5120 output rows. MMVQ launches one grid row per input row, so its cost is linear in the number of input rows, while MMQ (`ggml_mul_mat_a8`) has a fixed cost that a very large matrix amortizes. For a large-vocab lm_head this makes the 2-row case (e.g. the verify window of one-step speculative decoding) almost twice as slow as it needs to be.\n\nQ6_K lm_head of a 248K-vocab model under TP2 (124,160 x 2560 per rank), RTX 5070 Ti (sm_120), time per call inside a CUDA graph:\n\n| input rows | MMVQ | MMQ |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 324 µs | 378 µs |\n| 2 | 643 µs | 381 µs |\n| 3 | 963 µs | 385 µs |\n| 4 | 1284 µs | 387 µs |\n\nA mid-sized matrix behaves differently: an 8192 x 2560 Q6_K is still faster in MMVQ at 2 rows (25.6 µs vs 32.3 µs MMQ). So the existing rule is right for ordinary layers, and the change is a threshold on output rows.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/gguf.py`: add a module-level constant `MMVQ_SINGLE_ROW_ABOVE = 32768`. For non-I-Matrix types, a matrix with more than that many output rows uses MMVQ for a single input row only, and MMQ from 2 rows.\n- I-Matrix types are unchanged: they have no MMQ kernel, so leaving MMVQ would fall back to dequantization.\n- Nothing else in the dispatch changes; batch-size-1 decode still uses MMVQ everywhere.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nMMQ and MMVQ both quantize the activations to q8_1 and accumulate the same blocks, so the lm_head output differs only at bf16 rounding level. On the speculative-decoding run below, the draft acceptance length was unchanged (1.49 before and after), and generated text showed no quality change.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nEnd to end, measured as an A/B of this one change in our serving tree (SGLang with a KTransformers CPU/GPU hybrid MoE, so not upstream main itself): a Qwen-architecture IQ3_S GGUF model with a Q6_K lm_head (248K vocab), TP2 on 2x RTX 5070 Ti, one-step speculative decoding (2-row verify), Japanese fiction decode probe, mean of 8 runs:\n\n| | decode tok/s (mean) |\n|---|---|\n| without this change | 77.6 |\n| with this change | 80.8 |\n\nPer-call kernel times are in the table above. Without speculative decoding (1 row per step) the dispatch is unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). (ruff 0.15.1 format/check, isort 7.0.0)\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (dispatch-only change; no new kernel)\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (not needed)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37992976860](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37992976860)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37992976462](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37992976462)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37992976680](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37992976680)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
